    "Exceptional weather": "Erakordne ilm",
    "Simulation is active. ThermalPilot does not control heating.": "Simulatsioon on aktiivne. ThermalPilot ei juhi kütet.",
    "Observation and learning only; no thermostat control.": "Ainult vaatlus ja õppimine; juhtimist pole.",
    "ThermalPilot controls thermostat targets.": "ThermalPilot juhib termostaatide sihte.",
    "Seasonal fallback temperatures are used.": "Kasutatakse hooajalisi varutemperatuure.",
    "Scheduled targets remain simulated; season transitions can change thermostat targets.": "Plaan on simuleeritud; hooajavahetus võib muuta tegelikke sihte.",
    "Live thermostat control is not enabled.": "Tegelik juhtimine pole lubatud.",
    "Target changes include the shared start/stop offsets. The temperature forecast models the planned heating period; actual valve and heat-pump delays must be checked against observations.": "Sisaldab algus- ja lõpunihkeid. Kontrolli tegelikke ventiili- ja pumbaviivitusi vaatlustega.",
    "These forecasts were saved 1, 3 or 6 hours before the measurements. Later readings do not change them. Lower error is better; compare it with simply predicting no temperature change. Different heating, computers and other heat sources can affect the result.": "Prognoosid salvestati 1, 3 või 6 tundi enne mõõtmist ega muutu hiljem. Väiksem kõrvalekalle on parem; võrdle muutumatu temperatuuriga. Muud soojusallikad mõjutavad tulemust.",
    "Compare recorded temperatures with forecasts saved hours earlier. The accuracy cards also compare against predicting no temperature change. Forecasts assume the proposed heating plan; actual heating may differ, especially during simulation.": "Võrdle mõõtmisi varasemate prognooside ja muutumatu temperatuuriga. Tegelik küte võib eriti simulatsioonis plaanist erineda.",
    "Forecasts are compared with measurements within five minutes of their due time. “Similar heating” means observed demand matched the forecast for at least 90% of observations, with no large recording gaps. These counts give context, not a guarantee of accuracy.": "Mõõtmine viie minuti sees tähtajast. Sarnane küte: vähemalt 90% vastavus suurte lünkadeta. Arvud pole täpsuse garantii.",
    "Each row shows the latest observation within its 15-minute interval, not an average. Suggested thermostat target is the setting ThermalPilot would apply, not a room-temperature forecast. Table shows up to 288 intervals. Original observations remain stored internally. Short chart views use 15-minute time labels; longer views use wider intervals.": "Viimane vaatlus iga 15 minuti kohta, mitte keskmine. Siht on termostaadi seade, mitte prognoos. Kuni 288 intervalli; algandmed säilivad.",
    "Suggested On means the boosted target window, including valve timing offsets. Relay On means observed demand; it does not guarantee heat flow.": "Soovitatud sees on tõstetud siht ventiilinihetega. Relee sees näitab nõudlust, mitte tagatud soojusvoogu.",
    ", without heating, remaining slab warmth or appliance heat. Lower temperature loss means slower modeled cooling. This is a model estimate, not measured energy efficiency or an insulation rating.": ", ilma kütte, jääk- või seadmesoojuseta. Väiksem kadu tähendab mudelis aeglasemat jahtumist; see pole energia- ega soojustusnäitaja.",
    "Cooling-speed bands are provisional: under 1 h, 1–2 h, 2–4 h, 4–8 h, and 8 h or longer per 1°C drop. For a selected house type, badges instead compare with that type: under 0.5×, 0.5–0.8×, 0.8–1.25×, 1.25–2×, and at least 2× its reference cooling time. Initial rooms share starting estimates and remain unrated. Comparisons become more useful as their heat-loss parameters adapt to observations. Wind, ventilation, sensor placement and unmeasured heat sources can affect the estimates. The listed time describes this reference test, not how long heating can safely remain off in your home.": "Algmudelid on samad. Tuul, ventilatsioon, anduriasukoht ja muu soojus mõjutavad võrdlust. Võrdlusaeg pole ohutu küttepausi kestus.",
    "Learned parameters and season aggregates are retained when old observations are compacted.": "Õpitud parameetrid ja hooaja kokkuvõtted säilivad ajaloo tihendamisel.",
    "Open a Home Assistant dashboard once, then return here to load embedded history cards.": "Ava Home Assistanti töölaud ja naase ajaloo laadimiseks.",
    "Water-based systems only: raise the thermostat target this many minutes before the planned heat-delivery session, allowing slow valves to open. Electric and air distribution ignore this setting and use no advance offset.": "Ainult vesiküte: tõsta varem aeglaste ventiilide avamiseks. Elekter ja õhk eiravad nihet.",
    "Water-based systems only: lower the thermostat target this many minutes before the planned heat-delivery session ends, allowing valves to close. Electric and air distribution ignore this setting and use no closing offset.": "Ainult vesiküte: langeta enne lõppu ventiilide sulgemiseks. Elekter ja õhk eiravad nihet.",
    "What produces heat for your house. Select air-to-water for your water floor system supplied by an air-source heat pump. Gas, oil, wood and district heating need their own fuel-cost logic; choosing a house detail does not yet enable a different controller or reset learned room data.": "Maja soojusallikas. Kütusesüsteemidel puudub oma kulupõhine juhtimine; andmed säilivad.",
    "How heat reaches rooms: circulating water in floors or radiators, electric floor/ceiling/panels, or warm air. Mixed means different rooms use different systems. Water distribution can optionally use a heating-water sensor and uses valve timing. Electric and warm-air distribution ignore those inputs and learn response from observed thermostat demand. Mixed and Other retain water requirements until room overrides are supported.": "Soojusjaotus: vesi kasutab ventiiliaegu ja valikulist andurit; elekter ja õhk õpivad nõudlusest. Segatud säilitab veeseaded.",
    "The construction around floor heating, which affects how slowly heat is stored and released. Concrete slab describes your heated floor. Choose Not applicable if there is no floor heating. This does not change your configured response lag or erase learned parameters.": "Põrand mõjutab salvestamist. Põrandakütteta vali Ei kohaldu. Ei muuda viivitust ega mudelit.",
    "The structure below your home: slab on ground, crawl space or basement. A heated concrete floor can be above a basement, so this is separate from Heated floor. Choose Unknown if unsure. This descriptive setting does not reset observation history or learned models.": "Vundament on köetavast põrandast eraldi. Kahtluse korral vali Teadmata. Ajalugu ja mudelid säilivad.",
    "Sunlight through large windows, especially south-facing windows, can warm a room. No additional physical solar heating system is needed. Select the main direction of those windows to enable solar estimates, or Solar heating off to turn them off. Home Assistant’s location determines seasonal sun elevation and azimuth; cloud conditions come from your weather source. The effect starts at zero and learns gradually. Missing sunlight data assumes no solar warmth; room temperature limits still apply.": "Päike suurtest akendest, päikeseküttesüsteemi pole vaja. Suund ja asukoht annavad päikeseasendi, ilm pilved. Õpitakse nullist. Andmeteta päikesesoojust ei eeldata; piirid kehtivad.",
    "Clear means the windows receive direct sunlight without major obstructions. Choose Partly shaded for some trees, buildings or overhangs, or Mostly shaded when sunlight is usually blocked. Forecasts use a more cautious solar allowance: partly shaded uses 65% and mostly shaded 30% of the clear allowance. Actual room warming is still learned from observations; no solar heat is assumed before learning. Seasonal leaf cover and changing shading can still affect accuracy.": "Varjuta, osaline või tugev vari: prognoos kasutab 100%, 65% või 30% päikeselisast. Tegelik soojenemine õpitakse; vari võib muutuda.",
    "Optional local wind sensor, for example sensor.netatmo_tuuli_ms using m/s. Valid readings are averaged over the last 30 minutes. ThermalPilot learns a separate wind effect only after enough varied observations; no fixed wind penalty is assumed. Missing, invalid or unchanged-for-two-hours readings are ignored, and normal temperature-based planning and heating continue. Fresh wind correction gradually returns to typical conditions in forecasts further ahead. A stable calm reading may also be ignored conservatively. Units are detected automatically.": "Valikuline tuul, automaatsed ühikud ja 30 min keskmine. Õpitakse vahelduvatest andmetest. Puuduvad, vigased või 2 h muutumatud näidud eiratakse; küte jätkub. Kaugprognoos läheneb tavatuulele.",
    "Emergency lower temperature limit shared by all rooms. Each room’s own target is the normal comfort goal. ThermalPilot prioritizes avoiding this limit even when electricity is expensive; this value is not the idle thermostat target.": "Absoluutne alampiir, mitte puhkesiht. Toa siht on mugavus; piir kaitstakse ka kallitel tundidel.",
    "Upper temperature limit shared by all rooms. Extra heating and heat storage must stay within this limit.": "Kõigi tubade ülempiir; lisaküte ja varu ei tohi ületada.",
    "Optional sensor with forecast timestamp/value entries, such as Nordpool Predict FI. Only relative expensive/cheap patterns after confirmed prices are used, so no forecast price unit or additional costs are required. The Source price unit setting applies only to the confirmed total-price sensor. An expensive upcoming period can increase the heat reserve at the end of the known-price plan. Forecast prices are not compared directly with your total prices, used as confirmed prices or used to execute future heating commands. Missing forecasts keep normal planning. Confirmed prices always determine the executable schedule.": "Valikuline hinnatrend pärast kinnitatud hindu. Ühikut ega lisakulu pole vaja. Võib suurendada varu; ei ole kinnitatud hind ega tulevane juhtkäsk. Puudumisel tavaline plaan.",
    "Notify in Home Assistant when a room temperature sensor stays unchanged or unavailable for this many hours. A stable room can also have an unchanged reading, so the warning asks you to check the sensor. ThermalPilot sends at most one sensor notification per calendar day. Monitoring runs while ThermalPilot is active; long monitoring gaps restart the timer.": "Hoiata pärast seda aega muutumatu või puuduva temperatuuri korral.",
    "Summer fallback always applies from 15.5. through 30.9. Outside those dates, it also applies when the day’s lowest forecast temperature is equal to or above this value. For example, a setting of 6°C means the daily minimum must be at least 6°C for ThermalPilot to use summer fallback temperatures. Lower readings already observed that day are included. If a full-day forecast is unavailable outside the summer dates, winter fallback is used.": "Suverežiim 15.5.–30.9. või täieliku päevaprognoosi miinimumi korral üle piiri. Puuduv prognoos väljaspool perioodi suve ei aktiveeri.",
    "Negative values reduce estimated heat loss while the fireplace is active; −20% means a 20% reduction.": "Negatiivne väärtus vähendab soojuskadu kamina kasutamisel; −20% tähendab 20% vähem.",
    "Prefer a sensor that includes electricity prices and additional costs, such as VAT, transfer tariffs, electricity tax and retailer margin. A variable electricity-price sensor without these costs also works. If transfer tariffs differ between day and night, including them helps ThermalPilot choose the cheapest heating hours; omitting them can shift heating to hours that are less economical overall. Select a source containing today/tomorrow or timestamped raw_today/raw_tomorrow price lists, and choose the matching source price unit.": "Eelista koguhinda maksude, ülekande ja marginaaliga. Muutuv hind ilma lisadeta töötab ka; päeva/öö ülekandetariifi puudumine võib tundide valikut halvendada. Kasuta today/tomorrow või ajatempliga raw_today/raw_tomorrow ja õiget ühikut.",
    "Hourly average uses fixed hourly averages of the source prices. 15 minutes plans using quarter-hour intervals. Flexible builds heating sessions in 15-minute steps, allowing runs such as 60 or 75 minutes while respecting the minimum flexible heating run.": "Tunni keskmine, 15 min intervall või paindlikud 15 min sammud minimaalse kestusega.",
    "The shortest planned heating session in flexible scheduling mode. Longer sessions can be chosen in 15-minute steps. This setting applies to flexible runs; valve opening and closing offsets are applied separately.": "Vähim paindlik kütteperiood; pikemad 15 min sammudega.",
    "Initial estimate of how slowly heat input affects room temperature and how long its effect persists. Concrete slabs often need a longer delay, but lightweight floors, radiators, electric heaters and air systems also have a response time. Use a shorter value for faster systems. This remains relevant to every distribution; it is separate from valve opening or closing time.": "Esialgne soojusinertsi ja jääkmõju hinnang; mudel õpib tegeliku reaktsiooni.",
    "The warm outdoor endpoint of the initial heating-hours curve. At this temperature or warmer, the starting model assumes the lower daily heating need. This curve seeds the model before enough real heating and cooling observations are available.": "Algmudeli päevase küttevajaduse soe piir; tegelik reaktsioon õpitakse.",
    "The cold outdoor endpoint of the initial heating-hours curve. At this temperature or colder, the starting model assumes the higher daily heating need. Set it below the warm endpoint. Actual room response is learned from observations.": "Algmudeli külm piir peab olema soojast madalam; tegelik reaktsioon õpitakse.",
    "Allows real thermostat setpoint changes when ThermalPilot changes between Active and Passive. Active applies each room’s target temperature; Passive applies the seasonal fallback: the shared summer setpoint or each room’s normal target in winter. These commands can occur even with simulation enabled. This does not enable live heating schedule control.": "Lubab tegelikud hooajamuutused ka simulatsioonis: aktiivne toa siht, passiivne suve/talve varu. Ei luba ajakavade juhtimist.",
    "The thermostat target used for all configured rooms while ThermalPilot is Passive, if real Active/Passive season setpoint control is enabled. A low summer target normally prevents heating without switching off the thermostats.": "Ühine suvesiht passiivsel hooajalisel juhtimisel. Madal siht väldib kütet termostaate välja lülitamata.",
    "Degrees added to each room’s target temperature during a suggested heating window. For example, a 20 °C target with a 1.5 °C boost suggests a 21.5 °C thermostat setpoint to store heat. Scheduled targets remain simulated in this version.": "Kraadid üle toa sihi soojuse salvestamiseks, nt 20 + 1,5 = 21,5°C.",
    "Negative values temporarily lower the thermostat target during expensive electricity hours. After a planned heating session, ThermalPilot first restores the room’s normal target. It then chooses reduction only when predicted stored warmth can avoid thermostat heating while supporting room comfort. For example, −1°C allows a 20°C target to be reduced to 19°C during selected costly hours. The reduced target never goes below Minimum allowed temperature. Normal target is restored when reduction is no longer useful; a new planned heating session uses the boosted target. Duration is chosen by the plan, not a fixed number of hours.": "Negatiivne alandus vaid kallitel tundidel piisava varuga. Pärast kütet esmalt tavaline siht. Mitte alla miinimumi; taastub kasu lõppedes. Kestuse valib plaan.",
    "Select the measured supply-water temperature. A temperature sensor uses its state; a climate entity uses its current_temperature attribute. This is the measured water temperature, not the thermostat’s target. Optional for water-based systems. A valid reading adjusts the estimated heating output. Without it, planning and learning continue from observed thermostat demand, without a water-temperature adjustment. Missing readings do not force fallback targets.": "Valikuline mõõdetud pealevool; climate kasutab current_temperature, mitte sihti. Korrigeerib võimsust. Puudumine ei peata plaani ega õppimist ega sunni varurežiimi.",
    "Simulation calculates heating suggestions without applying scheduled targets. Disable simulation and confirm to enable real thermostat control. If another automation controls these thermostats, disable it first. Observation and learning continue in both modes.": "Simulatsioon ei rakenda ajakava sihte. Tegelikuks juhtimiseks keela ja kinnita; lülita olemasolev kattuv automaatika välja. Õppimine jätkub mõlemas.",
    "Choose the interface language. Room and entity names remain unchanged. Save settings to keep the choice. Embedded history cards follow this choice where supported by Home Assistant.": "Vali keel ja salvesta. Tubade ja olemite nimed ei muutu. Manustatud ajalugu järgib keelt, kui toetatud.",
    "All room timelines share the price chart’s time axis.${zones.length?' Zone rows show recorded heating and cooling only; off and standby periods stay empty. Plan adds suggested heating only for tariff-optimized zones.':''} Teal shows the suggested thermostat boost window; amber shows observed heating demand. ": "Ühine ajatelg. Türkiis: soovitatud tõstmine; oranž: vaadeldud nõudlus. ",
    "The selected period controls past history. Today and tomorrow are included when prices are published. Recorded activity is shown before now; future suggestions follow the current plan. Price gaps stay empty. ": "Periood määrab ajaloo; täna ja homme hindade olemasolul. Enne: vaatlused; pärast: praegune plaan. Hinnalüngad tühjad. ",
    "Times align to 15-minute boundaries; wider views show fewer labels. Hover, focus or tap a price bar or heating period for details.": "15 min piirid; pikemates vaadetes vähem silte. Üksikasjad hiire, fookuse või puudutusega.",
    "This measures initial data collection, not model trustworthiness. Continue validating forecasts and heating suggestions before enabling live control. Learning continues after initial data collection.": "Algkogumine ei mõõda usaldusväärsust. Kontrolli prognoose ja soovitusi enne juhtimist; õppimine jätkub.",
    "History collection and learning paused because outdoor temperature is unavailable. Existing model parameters are retained.": "Ajalugu ja õppimine peatatud: välistemperatuur puudub. Mudel säilib.",
    "No weather forecast: current outdoor temperature is held constant.": "Ilmaprognoos puudub; praegune välistemperatuur hoitakse konstantsena.",
    "Live control awaits confirmation. Enable simulation, save, then disable it and confirm to activate thermostat control.": "Juhtimine ootab kinnitust. Luba simulatsioon, salvesta, siis keela ja kinnita.",
    "Waiting for enough heating and idle observations to estimate the remaining time.": "Ajahinnanguks oodatakse rohkem kütte- ja puhkevaatlusi.",
    "A door/window contact sensor can monitor the fireplace damper position. Select the sensor state that means the fireplace is in use. For a damper contact sensor, Open normally means active and Closed means inactive. Door/window labels are converted to Home Assistant’s underlying on/off values. Other sensors show their declared options, current valid state and any saved value. A contact state indicates the damper position; it does not prove that a fire is burning.": "Ukse-/aknakontakt siibril: Avatud tavaliselt aktiivne, Suletud mitteaktiivne. Salvestatakse on/off. Muud andurid näitavad olekuid. Siibri asend ei tõenda põlevat tuld.",
